{"at_utc": "2026-11-16T21:28:40.081610+00:00", "kind": "c1_lot_reallocation", "label": "after pilot: C.2a N=1000 infeasible in budget (signalled, no verdict for C.2a, no substitution); lot reallocation, total unchanged", "lot": "C.PILOT", "payload": {"decision_per_norm_s6": "C.2a at N=1000 is NOT executed (budget); it is signalled. No point is substituted: C.2a receives NO verdict. C.2a at N=100 (3 seeds) is executed as planned and evaluated descriptively in the final campaign (scaling point and comparison), never as a verdict. The tranche verdict is that of the CVAL-leading system among the systems with a retained point N=1000 (C.1, C.2b). Recorded before any training run.", "finding": "single-thread step time C.1 0.94 s, C.2b 0.93 s, C.2a 13.0 s (whole public past; graphs and sequence ~4x longer each); C.2a at N=1000 projects ~20 000 CPU s per seed, ~60 000 CPU s for 3 seeds, > the whole 17 400 s envelope even with 4 parallel processes", "lot_reallocation": {"C.TRAIN.100": [1100, 3000], "C.TRAIN.1000": [9900, 6000], "reason": "C.2a at N=100 costs ~2 100 s per seed (3 in parallel); C.1 and C.2b at N=1000 need ~2 800 s wall", "total_envelope_unchanged_s": 17400}, "pilot": "evidence/howm2_c1/PILOT.json (ledger #14)", "question_for_user": "Do you want, in a later mandate, a separate budget for C.2a at N=1000 (about 60 000 CPU s, i.e. ~4.5 h wall on 4 cores), or should C.2a be redefined/abandoned? Not needed to finish palier 1 as recorded here."}, "previous_sha256": "875a989642a4e4de008b5669853334a6afac4fd486bc055b945c2fcc9e44fff0", "record_sha256": "e1ac381bd2cc895c3ddae740d583d0f3106f2579327b4c5e2bb3696d06191a58", "sequence": 15, "wall_seconds": 0.0}
